# Copy ownership

User-facing wording lives in `@fuck-shorts/i18n` (`packages/i18n`). Website components stay thin: they import and render. They do not own the attitude.

- Copy changes land in `packages/i18n` (one file per voice under `src/voice/`, plus brand + voices registry).
- Do not add new user-facing English strings inside `apps/website` components, pages, or OG markup.
- “i18n” here means English diction / style voices (`genalpha`, `genz`, `millennial`, `boomer`, `shakespeare`, `oldtimey`, `pirate`, `computer`, `ai`, `reptile`, `generic`), not additional languages.

No regex — that is already a repo-wide coding standard.
